   "topic": "Supported source and value-list types for record_flow_output",
   "members": [
    "r2.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    2
   ],
   "questions": [
    "Must record_flow_output be restricted to a MappedListSource containing an AssembledValueList, or must it handle an AssembledFileList without accessing a StoredValue that does not exist?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "run_values"
   ],
   "id": "run_values:T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "judged_before",
    "quotes": [],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "This asks the same question as P1 on unchanged text.",
    "precedent": {
     "id": "P1",
     "round": "round-57",
     "topic": "Whether record_flow_output supports AssembledFileList by returning SpooledFilesRef or restricts sources to AssembledValueList",
     "kind": "answered",
     "quotes": [
      "A RecordedSource MUST answer a StoredValuesRef with its ref's value_id and port the source's port, the flow output port's name; a MappedListSource MUST publish its list's StoredValue with put_value_bytes and write it in one RecordDeliveryValuesChange through record_change under the given actor before answering its ref; it checks nothing, since a flow output holds the value its edge delivered and is of value carriage (A05 rule 7).",
      "Returns the StoredValuesRef named by the flow output port's name."
     ],
     "why": "The flow-output rule explicitly limits the operation to value carriage and requires a StoredValuesRef, so an AssembledFileList is not a supported record_flow_output source."
    },
    "verified": true,
    "blocking": false
   }
  }
 ],
